From 0ece69e7b5313b69439fa98cf8ad07024a1a3d1a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 23:17:53 -0700
Subject: Show the Bitcoin header parser does not accept a V2 header

Feed a 134-byte Lotus V2 header to the inherited CBlockHeader unserializer.
The read stops after the 80-byte prefix and leaves 54 bytes, so that prefix
read is not acceptance of a V2 block. The double-SHA256 of the prefix is not
the V2 header id. The V2 parser still returns the original fields and rejects
a 133-byte buffer without modifying its output.
---
 src/lotus_v2/CMakeLists.txt           |  15 +++
 src/lotus_v2/test_header_boundary.cpp | 144 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 159 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 src/lotus_v2/test_header_boundary.cpp

